  "limitations": [
    "QoolQit is opt-in under PASQAL MIT-derived terms including a patent grant limited to internal research or academic use; it is not labeled standard MIT.",
    "Perceval MIT includes an Exqalibur Python-bindings combination exception. The adapter computes lossless ideal Fock probabilities without sampling, loss, postselection or distinguishability.",
    "IQM static fake-device topology/noise models are not live hardware calibration. The pinned fake backend ignores seed_simulator, so Aer is called explicitly with the IQM noise model and seed.",
    "Alice & Bob models gate-level encoded cat-qubit noise, not a bosonic master equation. Qiskit 1.x is isolated; upstream unsupported macOS CRY/RCCX/RCCCX are excluded.",
    "Pulser and QoolQit retain actual 1 ns sampling and rounding. Continuous-ideal constant-drive errors include grid endpoints, not just ODE tolerances; maximum observed asymmetric 3-atom amplitude difference was 8.878e-4.",
    "Pulser phase convention differs from Bloqade by a phase sign and their fixed Rb C6 constants differ. These adapters return the actual SDK model and do not normalize or clip states.",
    "The deprecated but still public pinned QutipEmulator API is used because it exposes solver tolerances/raw states; upgrading it requires renewed interface verification.",
    "Only this macOS arm64 host was executed. Passing numerical regressions, protocol tests or independent code review is not final scientific Acceptance."
  ],
